{
  "note": [
    "The Observation Deck's fabric (DR-113), cut from the one tower layout in scripts/fabric-tower.mjs -- regenerate from there, do not hand-edit. OBSERVATION-DECK.metadata.json v2, and its one measured fact: the Tower Core's own drum IS this room's inner wall and the core's south-west gap IS its doorway. Put the core's axis 9.27 m north-east of this eye and the gap's centre lands on [4.15, -4.15], which is where v1 had already put the doorway. Everything else follows from it -- the parapet on an arc of radius 11.5 about the same axis, passing 2.23 m south-west of the eye, 1.1 m of coping with a pipe rail to 1.35; the terrace the crown's open south-west quadrant, about 8 m from drum to rail; the crown's enclosed mass standing to 8 m either side of it with the walkway narrowing past it and carrying on round.",
    "NOT ROOFED: the package's 8 m is that crown wall behind the eye, not a ceiling, so the up cap is sky with the drum and the wall up one side of it and, 30 m over it, the Helipad's deck on its narrower shaft. Down, the tower runs 457 m to the island's plateau and the sea lies at -500; the complex 500 m below is PAINTED, not modelled. The sea disc is 40 km, not the kit's 30, because the camera's far plane is 40 km (DR-109) and only a disc that reaches it puts the horizon the 0.72 degrees below level that 500 m really gives.",
    "North-east through the doorway, the core: its curved wall, its radial floor, the stair due west of its centre with its warm lamp, the cool lamp overhead -- and straight on through the core's north-east gap, the passage and a strip of the Comm Room's north-east wall, since this eye, the core's axis and both gaps lie on one 45-degree line. The elevator door is not in sight (bearing 33 from this eye, outside the doorway's 38 to 52). One sun for the whole tower: bearing 235, elevation 35, which is the day phase's and not a part here."
  ],
